direction: down

title: |md
  ## Sleepable BPF programs
| {near: top-center; shape: text}

normal: "Normal BPF program (NOT sleepable)" {
  style.fill: "#fee2e2"
  n_body: |md
    Atomic / non-faultable context:
    - kprobe in IRQ handler
    - tracepoint inside scheduler
    - XDP in NAPI softirq

    **Cannot:**
    - call helpers that page-fault
    - call helpers that block
    - acquire normal mutexes

    **Cannot use:**
    - bpf_copy_from_user (faults)
    - bpf_ima_inode_hash (crypto)
    - bpf_d_path (faults on dentry)
  |
}

sleepable: "Sleepable BPF program (SEC suffix .s/)" {
  style.fill: "#dcfce7"
  s_body: |md
    Faultable context:
    - fentry.s (sleepable trampoline)
    - lsm.s (sleepable LSM hook)
    - tracing iter
    - sk_lookup, cgroup{,_skb}.s

    **Can:**
    - bpf_copy_from_user (may fault)
    - bpf_d_path (may schedule)
    - longer-running operations
    - some allocators

    **Plumbing:**
    - protected by SRCU (not RCU)
    - may yield, may run for ms
  |
}

decl: "Declaration adds .s/ to the SEC name" {
  style.fill: "#fef3c7"
  decl_body: |md
    ```c
    SEC("fentry.s/__x64_sys_openat")
    /*       ^^ .s/ suffix == sleepable */
    ```
  |
}

normal -> sleepable -> decl
